WEBVTT

1
00:00:11.298 --> 00:00:13.600
My brother and I had a fight today.

2
00:00:14.701 --> 00:00:17.523
Alex is only two years older than I am.

3
00:00:17.923 --> 00:00:20.304
But he always tries to boss me around!

4
00:00:21.945 --> 00:00:24.107
The fight started with Mom's note.

5
00:00:26.108 --> 00:00:29.691
Dear Annie and Alex, Please clean Polly's cage.

6
00:00:30.211 --> 00:00:31.532
I'll be back before dinner!

7
00:00:38.373 --> 00:00:40.235
We both love our parrot.

8
00:00:41.436 --> 00:00:51.384
Polly has pretty feathers and says funny But we hate cleaning her cage.

9
00:00:52.565 --> 00:00:53.606
I looked at Alex.

10
00:00:55.228 --> 00:00:57.690
"Somebody has to clean the birdcage."

11
00:00:58.991 --> 00:00:59.732
He smirked.

12
00:01:01.524 --> 00:01:02.845
"It looks pretty nasty.

13
00:01:03.105 --> 00:01:04.165
Good luck scrubbing it!"

14
00:01:04.185 --> 00:01:09.347
"I cleaned it last week," I said.

15
00:01:09.367 --> 00:01:12.489
"It's your turn, Alex."

16
00:01:12.509 --> 00:01:17.691
"Can't!" he said as he walked to the door.

17
00:01:17.711 --> 00:01:21.412
"I have to practice my skills.

18
00:01:21.892 --> 00:01:24.313
So I'm going outside to shoot some hoops.

19
00:01:24.774 --> 00:01:25.494
Have fun!"

20
00:01:25.514 --> 00:01:28.775
"Happy Birthday!"

21
00:01:29.275 --> 00:01:30.396
Polly squawked.

22
00:01:31.308 --> 00:01:34.751
"Ugh," I thought, looking at her dirty cage.

23
00:01:35.492 --> 00:01:37.013
Alex was so mean.

24
00:01:38.354 --> 00:01:40.156
He was so selfish too.

25
00:01:40.776 --> 00:01:43.699
There was no way I was cleaning the cage again!

26
00:01:49.824 --> 00:01:53.647
Outside I heard his basketball bouncing on the driveway.

27
00:01:56.389 --> 00:02:05.378
Suddenly I had an idea My younger sister is so annoying.

28
00:02:06.818 --> 00:02:11.401
She's only two years younger than I am, but she acts like a big baby.

29
00:02:11.421 --> 00:02:16.364
Mom said somebody had to clean Polly's cage.

30
00:02:17.805 --> 00:02:21.186
I didn't mind doing it, but I do it all the time.

31
00:02:22.687 --> 00:02:25.109
So I asked Annie to take a turn.

32
00:02:26.469 --> 00:02:30.672
Of course, Annie started whining and complaining—as usual.

33
00:02:32.440 --> 00:02:34.681
"I hate cleaning the birdcage!"

34
00:02:34.701 --> 00:02:38.482
"Well, it's your turn, Annie.

35
00:02:39.462 --> 00:02:42.803
Mom is going to be home soon, so you'd better get started."

36
00:02:45.884 --> 00:02:48.284
"I'm not cleaning the birdcage!"

37
00:02:48.604 --> 00:02:49.265
she yelled.

38
00:02:54.186 --> 00:02:54.866
are so!"

39
00:02:55.306 --> 00:02:57.607
I told her as she stormed upstairs.

40
00:02:57.627 --> 00:03:02.088
"Uh-oh!" Polly squawked at me.

41
00:03:03.968 --> 00:03:06.590
"Annie is such a baby," I muttered.

42
00:03:10.212 --> 00:03:12.734
I went outside and practiced slam dunks.

43
00:03:18.398 --> 00:03:18.898
I thought.

44
00:03:18.918 --> 00:03:21.760
"Hey, Annie.

45
00:03:22.200 --> 00:03:32.767
I've got an idea When I got home, Alex and Annie were in the driveway playing basketball.

46
00:03:35.165 --> 00:03:35.985
"Hi, kids.

47
00:03:36.466 --> 00:03:38.187
Did you clean the birdcage?"

48
00:03:38.708 --> 00:03:39.248
I asked.

49
00:03:39.268 --> 00:03:42.171
"Yep," said Alex.

50
00:03:44.373 --> 00:03:46.535
"We did it together," said Annie.

51
00:03:46.555 --> 00:03:50.058
"Really?" I said.

52
00:03:50.078 --> 00:03:53.180
"I thought you two would argue about it!"

53
00:03:53.200 --> 00:03:57.664
"We had a foul shooting contest," said Alex.

54
00:03:57.684 --> 00:04:01.608
"The loser was supposed to clean the cage."

55
00:04:04.748 --> 00:04:07.951
"But we each scored five points," said Annie.

56
00:04:07.971 --> 00:04:12.916
"So—" "You cleaned the cage together!"

57
00:04:13.476 --> 00:04:14.697
I said, hugging them.

58
00:04:18.281 --> 00:04:19.322
Polly squawked.

59
00:04:19.342 --> 00:04:20.963
"Good job, team!"
